Everything aligns to a 8 px grid, content max-width = 360 px mobile, 420 px desktop.

2 · Component Anatomy & Tailwind Classes
Zone	Element	Key Classes
Card shell	<article>	relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900
Photo	<Image> 4:5	w-full aspect-[4/5] object-cover
Gradient overlay	<div>	absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[30%] bg-gradient-to-t from-black/60 to-transparent
Info section	<section>	p-4 space-y-1 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50
Heading	Name + breed	flex items-center gap-1 font-semibold text-lg
Meta row	age,size,distance	text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400
Bio	2-line clamp	line-clamp-2 text-sm
Compatibility badge	<span>	inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-600/10 text-emerald-700 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium
Action buttons wrapper	<div>	flex justify-center gap-7 py-3
Action button	<motion.button>	rounded-full p-4 shadow-md bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 transition
3 · Spacing & Sizing Rules
Base unit = 8 px
Card padding: 2 units (16 px)
Gap between buttons: 3 units (24 px)
Text
Name line: font-semibold / 1.2
Meta + bio: text-sm + leading-5
Buttons
Icon 24×24 inside 64×64 circle
Colours:
pass ⇦ neutral-400
like ♡ rose-500 → rose-600 on hover
super-like ➜ sky-500 → sky-600 on hover
Safe-Area Insets
On iOS devices, add bottom padding pb-safe class (env(safe-area-inset-bottom)).
4 · Motion & Feedback
tsx
<motion.button
  whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}
  whileTap={{ scale: 0.9 }}
  transition={{ type: 'spring', stiffness: 300, damping: 20 }}
/>
Haptics: navigator.vibrate?.(8) on like / super-like (mobile).
Sound (optional): play subtle “pop” mp3 on action.
5 · Responsive Behaviour
Breakpoint	Max card width	Button size
≤ sm (640)	100 % – 32 px side padding	56 px
md (768)	360 px	64 px
lg (1024)	420 px	72 px
Use mx-auto and Tailwind container utilities.

6 · Implementation Steps
Create new component SwipeCardV2.tsx → keep V1 until stable.
Refactor old props to data-object shape:
ts
type PetCardData = {
  id: string
  name: string
  breed: string
  age: number
  size: 'tiny'|'small'|'medium'|'large'
  distanceKm: number
  bio: string
  photos: string[]
  compatibility?: number
}
Migrate CSS – remove inline styles; rely on Tailwind.
Replace action handlers with prop callbacks:
tsx
onSwipe('like'|'pass'|'superlike', pet.id)
Update pages (/swipe etc.) to import SwipeCardV2.
7 · Quick Visual Regression Test
ts
import { render } from '@testing-library/react'
import { SwipeCardV2 } from '../SwipeCardV2'
import { toMatchImageSnapshot } from 'jest-image-snapshot'

expect.extend({ toMatchImageSnapshot })

it('renders consistent layout', async () => {
  const { container } = render(<SwipeCardV2 pet={mockPet}/>)

  const png = await html2canvas(container).then(c => c.toDataURL())
  expect(Buffer.from(png.split(',')[1], 'base64')).toMatchImageSnapshot()
})
8 · Common Pitfalls
Aspect-ratio – always object-cover; otherwise photo stretches.
Button overlap – ensure wrapper outside relative photo div.
Bio length – use line-clamp-2 (@tailwindcss/line-clamp plugin).
Dark-mode text – test contrast on both themes (WCAG AA).
RTL languages – confirm padding & icon direction via dir="rtl" toggle.
